Subject: [PATCH] Phase 6 Milestone 6 - Knowledge Graph Foundation (GEN-0025)

Production implementation of the existing src.services.memory.interfaces.
KnowledgeGraph Protocol, which had only InMemoryKnowledgeGraph (explicitly
documented as 'not production storage') until now. Built entirely on
existing architecture: the KnowledgeGraph Protocol itself (unmodified),
DatabaseSessionManager (Phase 4.2), and the SQLAlchemyRepository/di_wire.py
DI pattern already established for tasks/events. Kernel and Agent isolation
both preserved -- src/core/ and src/runtime/ diffs are empty; only
src/storage/ files were touched.

src/storage/models.py (extended, StorageRecord unchanged): added
GraphNodeRecord and GraphEdgeRecord. Dedicated tables rather than reusing
the generic StorageRecord document store, because neighbors() needs to
filter edges by indexed source_id/relation columns -- a JSON blob can't
do that efficiently.

src/storage/knowledge_graph.py (new): SQLAlchemyKnowledgeGraph, backed by
SQLite or PostgreSQL via the existing DatabaseSessionManager -- no new
per-dialect code, exactly like SQLAlchemyRepository. add_node() upserts by
id, matching the storage layer's existing upsert convention. neighbors()
matches InMemoryKnowledgeGraph's exact semantics: only nodes explicitly
added via add_node() surface as neighbors (an edge to a never-declared id
does not), and duplicate edges to the same target are deduplicated while
preserving insertion order.

src/storage/di_wire.py (extended, no existing registration changed):
registers KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH depending on the existing DB_SESSION_MANAGER,
and adds it to RepositoryRegistry under 'knowledge_graph' -- the seven
existing registry entries (tasks/events/memory/sql_tasks/sql_events/
redis_cache/short_term_memory/vector_memory) are all unchanged.

Dependency Injection only throughout: SQLAlchemyKnowledgeGraph takes a
DatabaseSessionManager constructor argument, built and wired the same way
every other Phase 4.2+ backend is -- no new construction pattern
introduced. No breaking API: KnowledgeGraph Protocol itself untouched, so
InMemoryKnowledgeGraph and SQLAlchemyKnowledgeGraph remain interchangeable
with no caller changes.

11 new/updated tests (10 in tests/unit/storage/test_knowledge_graph.py,
1 new case plus 1 extended case in test_di_wire.py), 100% coverage on
both knowledge_graph.py and models.py, including a Protocol conformance
check.

Verified: ruff check, ruff format --check, mypy --strict src (60 files),
pytest (220 passed, up from 210; 96% coverage) all clean. src/core/ and
src/runtime/ diffs are both empty.
